 "notes": "Digitised from Fig. 1 (mainlim.jpeg in the e-print) of Witte & Mummery, arXiv:2412.03655: 2-sigma black-hole superradiance exclusion on the axion decay constant from the inferred spins of Cyg X-1 (conservative spin inference) and GRS 1915+105, computed with n<=5 superradiant levels. The figure plots 1/f_a [GeV^-1] vs m_a [eV] directly, so no conversion was applied. The reported curve is the upper boundary of the paper's fiducial (dark blue) excluded region, which covers the m<=2 spin-down region (m_a ~ 1.8e-13 to 6.0e-12 eV); the excluded region extends below the curve to arbitrarily small 1/f_a (first and last points close the region at the plot floor, 1/f_a ~ 1e-18 GeV^-1). The lighter shaded extension up to m_a ~ 1.1e-11 eV (m>2 spin-down, potentially altered by higher-order levels) was NOT included. Axis calibration from major tick pixels (262 px/decade in m_a, 123.4 px/decade in 1/f_a). Limit is astrophysical (BH spins), independent of the local dark-matter density.",
